      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bafbca9282d5d55fb6899f8|full_name}: same,\nMIne row is like all down the bottom, so are my favorites.\nno i don't want to see udon world and the same old \"HOT\" world that's been there for the last year... but that's beside the point.\ni'm amazed that some things like VKET gets their own row, while being a larger event i understand that, but it happens twice a year, while nightclub-type of events happens multiple times a week, and have been for well over a year now.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-07T22:30:01.101Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "pretty self explanatory. we dance communities are driving at least 10% of the player base, yet finding club worlds for new comers is always a hit or miss. we often have over hundreds of people at community events every weekend. i think this should be reflected by VRChat by promoting the virtual clubbing scene. it wouldn't be too hard to add to the world menu as a dedicated row, which in turn would make it easier for people to find active instances of dancing events \n\nedit: to be clear, we are talking about SFW dance events here. no lapdancing or stripclubs events (those are always invite only, anyways)",
